% Probe: the vertical extent a `+code` block occupies, and where its contents
% sit inside it.
%
% Body text is CJK on purpose: the two engines' font descriptors agree for the
% japanese face (19.36 vs 19.34) and disagree for the latin one, so a CJK
% baseline is comparable ACROSS engines and a latin one is not. The code
% content itself is latin (lmmono) and is only ever compared engine-internally,
% against the frame rectangle the same engine drew.
@require: stdjabook
@require: code

document (|
  title = {code probe};
  author = {};
  show-title = false;
  show-toc = false;
|) '<
  +p{あいうえお。}
  +code(`one`);
  +p{かきくけこ。}
  +code(`two
three`);
  +p{さしすせそ。}
>
